  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 240 PM MDT Sun Sep 13 2026\n\nTuesday and into the weekend, the upper level low \nkeeps migrating east into the Great Lakes and Hudson Bay region. The \ncounter clockwise circulation will begin filtering cold air from the \nArctic into the region undergoing some warming/modification as it \npushes south over us. 700mb temperatures will drop between 8 and 12C \ntranslating daily surface temperatures into the cooler 60's and \n70's and overnight temperatures into the 40's and 50's. Daily \nrainfall chances start to occur Wednesday as a train of Low \npressure system system are expected to travel through the \nPacific Northwest over the next 7 days. This precession of low \npressure systems will push the ridge eastward into the central \nand southern plains leaving the intermountain west susceptible \nto multiple accompanied shortwaves but ahead and following each \nprogged low pressure system.",
